{"code":"47-2081.00","title":"Drywall and Ceiling Tile Installers","description":"Apply plasterboard or other wallboard to ceilings or interior walls of buildings. Apply or mount acoustical tiles or blocks, strips, or sheets of shock-absorbing materials to ceilings and walls of buildings to reduce or reflect sound. Materials may be of decorative quality. Includes lathers who fasten wooden, metal, or rockboard lath to walls, ceilings, or partitions of buildings to provide support base for plaster, fireproofing, or acoustical material.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":7,"share":0.5671},"I":{"score":1.96,"share":0.0907},"A":{"score":2.3,"share":0.1229},"S":{"score":1.18,"share":0.017},"E":{"score":1,"share":0},"C":{"score":3.14,"share":0.2023}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":13504,"text":"Read blueprints or other specifications to determine methods of installation, work procedures, or material or tool requirements.","core":true,"importance":4.41,"relevance":87.9,"frequency":5.54},{"id":13503,"text":"Measure and mark surfaces to lay out work, according to blueprints or drawings, using tape measures, straightedges or squares, and marking devices.","core":true,"importance":4.38,"relevance":88.8,"frequency":5.15},{"id":13512,"text":"Cut and screw together metal channels to make floor or ceiling frames, according to plans for the location of rooms or hallways.","core":true,"importance":4.2,"relevance":81.91,"frequency":4.45},{"id":13508,"text":"Hang drywall panels on metal frameworks of walls and ceilings in offices, schools, or other large buildings, using lifts or hoists to adjust panel heights, when necessary.","core":true,"importance":4.19,"relevance":97.42,"frequency":4.66},{"id":13505,"text":"Fit and fasten wallboard or drywall into position on wood or metal frameworks, using glue, nails, or screws.","core":true,"importance":4.18,"relevance":94.61,"frequency":4.93},{"id":13507,"text":"Measure and cut openings in panels or tiles for electrical outlets, windows